codex
The finite-sort shortcut exposed a prover limitation: it did not case-split an abstract enum variable, so that version correctly failed rather than certifying an uncovered branch. I’m switching the valid-input proof to a deterministic 64-case verification loop (all concrete pairs in one claim) and retaining symbolic claims for the invalid-name regions.
apply patch
